  [PASS] K5 THE LENSING KEEPER IS THE ONE WITH REAL TEETH, and it cuts BOTH ways.  The KiDS-1000 isolated-lens RAR reaches accelerations two decades below a_0, so an external field of the size h48 needs for the pairs is a large effect there.  Under eq. 60 the fit is destroyed at e_N = 0.03; under the flux theorem it degrades by about half as much.  Reported against interest: even at e_N = 0 this zero-parameter prediction is not a good fit on the published covariance, so the keeper being defended is 'the shape and amplitude to ~15%', not a chi2   (chi2 (11 points, no free parameter): e_N = 0 147.5; e_N = 0.0046 eq.60 833.0 vs flux 584.8; e_N = 0.03 eq.60 1071.5 vs flux 904.0)

