4.  THE BINARY-GALAXY GEOMETRY -- the fourth liability the brief names, rebuilt on 2MRS (h48/h69b's own sample)
============================================================================================================================
  2MRS pairs rebuilt: 1830 strictly isolated major pairs (d3 > 5 r_p), median r_p = 141 kpc, median log M_b = 11.20

  law                                              A = sigma_obs/sigma_pred      dex
  Milgrom exact isolated deep-MOND two-body               1.886 +/-  0.047    0.276
  EFE, naive nu(e_N) G          [h48's]                   2.298 +/-  0.057    0.361
  EFE, FLUX THEOREM orientation avg                       2.501 +/-  0.066    0.398
  EFE, eq. 60 along the field                             3.126 +/-  0.082    0.495
  h48 framework branch, min(deep-MOND, naive EFE)          2.618 +/-  0.062    0.418
  Newton, baryons only, no dark matter                    5.764 +/-  0.144    0.761
  LambdaCDM abundance-matched NFW (0 free par.)           0.949 +/-  0.023   -0.023
  [PASS] 4a THE BINARY LIABILITY IS UNTOUCHED BY THE EFE PRESCRIPTION, and for a structural reason.  The framework's best case here is already Milgrom's EXACT deep-MOND two-body law, derived from the virial relation with no prescription in it at all, and it needs A ~ 1.9.  Every external-field branch is WORSE than that, and the corrected prescription is worse than h48's naive one because it suppresses more than nu(e_N) alone.  There is no member of the family below the isolated branch, so the 19-sigma excess survives Angle C intact   (exact isolated deep-MOND A = 1.89 +/- 0.05 (18.8 sigma above unity); EFE branch at e_N = 0.03: naive 2.30, flux theorem 2.50, eq.60 3.13; LambdaCDM lands at 0.95 +/- 0.02 with nothing fitted)
  [PASS] 4b AND THE PAIRS ARE IN THE EFE-DOMINATED REGIME, which is what makes the isolated branch illegitimate rather than merely optimistic.  At the median separation the pair's own internal Newtonian field is far below the large-scale-structure field, so the correct QUMOND answer for these systems is the external-field branch -- the branch that fits worst.  The framework's published number comes from the branch its own geometry forbids   (median internal y = g_N/a_0 = 0.0114 against an assumed external 0.03; 70% of the pairs are external-field dominated)

