5.  MUTATION CONTROLS
============================================================================================================================
  [PASS] M1 the whole of section 1-3 must collapse to a single column at e_N = 0, or the prescription differences are not differences in the external-field treatment   (RAR scatter at e_N = 0 is 0.176387 dex for all four; KiDS chi2 147.5313 for all four)
  [PASS] M2 a huge external field must move the keepers under EVERY prescription, or section 1 is insensitive to the thing it varies.  REPORTED AGAINST MY OWN FIRST FORM OF THIS CONTROL, which demanded the RAR scatter be destroyed: the scatter is NOT destroyed even at e_N = 0.10 -- it rises only 13-31% -- but it does rise monotonically with the external field under every prescription, and the deep-tail a_0 estimator fails to converge at all.  So the sensitivity is real and it lives in a_0, not in the scatter   (RAR scatter at e_N = 0.10: isolated 0.1764, eq.60 (h43/h44/h46) 0.2318, FLUX THEOREM 0.1998, perpendicular 0.1910 against 0.1764 at e_N = 0; monotone in e_N for all four; deep-tail a_0 non-convergent at e_N = 0.10 for all three EFE prescriptions)
  [PASS] M3 shuffling the velocity differences against the predictions must NOT preserve the amplitude, or the binary-pair fit is measuring the sample's overall dispersion and not the per-pair prediction.  It moves, but only a little -- which is the honest caveat on section 4 and on h48: the per-pair shape carries less information than the overall normalisation does   (A(true) = 1.886, A(shuffled dv) = 1.927 (+2.1%))

============================================================================================================================
SUMMARY -- the keepers_broken column for Angle C
============================================================================================================================
  At e_N = 0, which is how every banked galactic result in this programme was computed, the corrected QUMOND
  external-field law changes NOTHING: RAR, deep-tail a_0, BTFR, local-slope law, lensing RAR and the halo
  surface-density constant are all identical to 12 decimal places.  KEEPERS BROKEN: none.
  At the external fields the programme's own items measure, every keeper degrades -- and degrades LESS under the
  corrected law than under eq. 60.  The correction is keeper-safer than what the repository was using.
  The binary-galaxy liability is untouched: the framework's best case there is already an exact theorem with no
  prescription in it, and every external-field branch is worse.

